  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1203 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nHot and dry conditions continue through the long term forecast. The \nupper ridging will continue to expand across the southeastern CONUS \nearly next week where it is expected to remain stagnant through the \nrest of the week. Models indicate an upper trough will swing across \nthe Desert Southwest early in the week, effectively pushing the \nridge a little farther east. However, conditions will remain dry and \nhot as our region will remain under the western edge of the ridge. \nThe upper trough will quickly absorb into northerly flow and the \nupper ridging will retreat back to the west. Forecast highs remain \nin the upper 90s to just below Heat Advisory criteria (105-109 \ndegrees) everyday next week. Subsidence below the upper ridging will \nkeep precipitation chances near zero. With hot temperatures and dry \nconditions, could see fire weather concerns return sometime next \nweek.",
